  "description": "MUXRUV crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C147 H106 Cl8 Dy7 N10 O41 1+,5(C1 H4 O1),C2 H3 N1,N1 O3 1-. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.512-3.936 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.79-113.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy7(OH)6(OMe)2(NO3)1.5(nacb)2(nacbH)6(MeOH)(H2O)2](NO3)1.5 (1·5MeOH·MeCN; air-dried 1·MeOH). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
